GPIO-001,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,Verify read/write of key GPIO registers with reset defaults and boundary values,Default pad mux; No interrupts enabled; All pads inputs by default,"GPIO_DIR, GPIO_DATA, GPIO_INT_EN, GPIO_INT_TYPE, GPIO_INT_POLARITY, GPIO_INT_STATUS, GPIO_DEBOUNCE",Clock/reset,1) Read reset values; 2) Write 0x0/0xFFFFFFFF patterns; 3) Read back and compare; 4) Write walking-1/0; 5) Read back; 6) Restore defaults,All register writes persist and readbacks match; No bus errors; Reset values match spec,[registers, smoke, gpio],Validation Team
GPIO-002,test_gpio_negedge_intr_en,Validate negative-edge interrupt enable on selected pad(s) and servicing flow,Pad mux selects GPIO; One pad driven externally with falling edge stimulus; NVIC/PLIC enabled for GPIO,"GPIO_INT_EN, GPIO_INT_TYPE, GPIO_INT_POLARITY, GPIO_INT_STATUS, GPIO_INT_CLEAR, GPIO_DIR, GPIO_DEBOUNCE",Interrupt controller routing; External stimulus generator,1) Configure pad as input; 2) Set INT_TYPE=edge, POLARITY=falling; 3) Enable INT_EN for pad; 4) Apply falling edge; 5) Wait ISR; 6) Read/clear INT_STATUS; 7) Deassert stimulus,ISR fires once; INT_STATUS bit set then cleared; No spurious interrupts; Debounce behavior per config,[interrupts, negedge, edge, gpio],Validation Team
GPIO-003,test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en,Validate positive-edge interrupt across all pads enabled simultaneously and check no missed/extra interrupts,Pad mux selects GPIO on all pads; Debounce optional; NVIC/PLIC enabled,"GPIO_INT_EN, GPIO_INT_TYPE, GPIO_INT_POLARITY, GPIO_INT_STATUS, GPIO_INT_CLEAR, GPIO_DIR, GPIO_DEBOUNCE",Interrupt controller routing; External pattern generator,1) Configure all pads as inputs; 2) Set INT_TYPE=edge, POLARITY=rising; 3) Enable INT_EN for all pads; 4) Apply rising edges to all pads; 5) Verify ISR count equals pad count; 6) Read/clear INT_STATUS bits; 7) Repeat with bursts,All pad interrupts observed exactly once per edge; No cross-talk; Status bits map to pads correctly,[interrupts, posedge, all-pads, gpio],Validation Team

